{#
  The attribution page for the openly-licensed stand-in photography.

  It EXISTS BECAUSE THE LICENCES REQUIRE IT. Nearly every picture in the
  case-study grids is CC BY-SA, which obliges us to name the photographer, name
  the licence and link to it. Cropping and grading them, which we do, counts as
  adapting them, so the obligation is ours and not the source's.

  Driven entirely from _data/imageCredits.js: delete a row there as each picture
  is replaced by our own photography, and when the list empties this page stops
  rendering itself rather than sitting here saying nothing.
#}
{% if imageCredits and imageCredits.length %}
    <!-- ===================== HERO (dark) ===================== -->
    <section class="section legal-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <h1 class="statement legal-hero__title">Photography <span class="em">credits.</span></h1>
        <p class="legal-hero__meta">Stand-in imagery, pending our own project photography</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== BODY (light) ===================== -->
    <section class="section section--light">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="legal-prose">
          <p class="legal-prose__lead">The photographs illustrating our case studies are stand-ins while our own project photography is prepared. They are not photographs of the work described, and where a client is anonymised we have deliberately used landscape rather than any identifiable property. Each one is used under an open licence, with thanks to the photographer.</p>

          <h2>Case study imagery</h2>
          <ul>
            {%- for c in imageCredits %}
            <li>
              <strong>{{ c.usedFor }}</strong>, standing in.
              <a href="{{ c.source }}" rel="noopener">{{ c.title }}</a>
              by {{ c.author }}{% if c.licence %}, {% if c.licenceUrl %}<a href="{{ c.licenceUrl }}" rel="license noopener">{{ c.licence }}</a>{% else %}{{ c.licence }}{% endif %}{% endif %},
              via Wikimedia Commons. Cropped and colour graded by us; the adaptation is offered under the same licence.
            </li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>

          <h2>Everything else</h2>
          <p>All other photography, the wordmark and the site design are our own or licensed for our use.</p>
          <p>If you are one of the photographers above and would like a credit corrected or a picture removed, please email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we will act on it promptly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
